  <h1 style="color: #d4af37; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px; text-transform: uppercase;">UAN Liquid Fertilizers</h1>
  <p style="text-align: center; color: #d4af37; font-size: 1.1em; margin-bottom: 30px;">HS Code: 310280</p>

  <p style="line-height: 1.8; font-size: 1.1em; margin-bottom: 20px; text-align: justify;">
    UAN (Urea Ammonium Nitrate) Liquid Fertilizers are highly efficient, stable aqueous solutions of urea and ammonium nitrate, providing a versatile combination of three nitrogen forms (nitrate, ammonium, and urea). SATCO supplies premium-grade UAN solutions designed for precision agriculture, offering exceptional uniformity, ease of handling, and compatibility with various pesticides and micronutrients for modern fertigation and foliar application systems.
  </p>

  <h2 style="color: #d4af37; border-bottom: 2px solid #d4af37; padding-bottom: 10px; margin-top: 40px;">Product Grades & Formulations</h2>
  <ul style="line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <li><strong>UAN-32 (Standard Export Grade):</strong> The most popular high-concentration formulation containing 32% total nitrogen, optimized for temperate climates and large-scale farming.</li>
    <li><strong>UAN-30 & UAN-28:</strong> Lower crystallization-temperature formulations engineered specifically for cooler weather application and winter crop management.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 style="color: #d4af37; border-bottom: 2px solid #d4af37; padding-bottom: 10px; margin-top: 40px;">Key Advantages</h2>
  <ul style="line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <li><strong>Multi-Form Nitrogen:</strong> Delivers immediate nitrate uptake, steady ammonium availability, and prolonged urea release for sustained crop nutrition.</li>
    <li><strong>Precise Application:</strong> Liquid form allows completely uniform field distribution, eliminating the striping or unevenness often associated with dry granular spreading.</li>
    <li><strong>Tank-Mix Flexibility:</strong> Easily mixes with herbicides, insecticides, and other liquid fertilizers, saving valuable time and labor costs.</li>
    <li><strong>Safe Handling & Storage:</strong> Non-pressurized solution stored safely at atmospheric pressure in specialized tanks.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 style="color: #d4af37; border-bottom: 2px solid #d4af37; padding-bottom: 10px; margin-top: 40px;">Primary Applications</h2>
  <ul style="line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <li><strong>Broad-Acre Field Crops:</strong> Extensively applied to corn, wheat, barley, sugar beets, and pastures using sprayers or injection knives.</li>
    <li><strong>Modern Irrigation Systems:</strong> Perfectly suited for center-pivot systems, drip irrigation, and micro-sprinklers (fertigation).</li>
    <li><strong>Stubble Breakdown:</strong> Applied directly to crop residues to accelerate microbial decomposition and enrich soil organic matter.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 style="color: #d4af37; border-bottom: 2px solid #d4af37; padding-bottom: 10px; margin-top: 40px;">Packaging & Supply Options</h2>
  <ul style="line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <li><strong>Bulk Chemical Tankers:</strong> Dedicated maritime and road transport vessels for large agricultural distributors.</li>
    <li><strong>ISO Tanks:</strong> Certified intermodal containers designed for secure international liquid logistics.</li>
    <li><strong>IBC Totes / Drums:</strong> Convenient medium-scale containment for regional agricultural supply centers.</li>
  </ul>

